 her from other people so she don't  really have any close friends and she  doesn't also have any close family her  mother victoria had died of cancer quite  young like many years before  so kenzie decides that her only recourse  in this situation is  she's gonna be forced to impose on her  only remaining family member her  grandmother shirley uh who again was  from the beginning of the book uh now  she's actually never met her  through her mom like before her mom died  uh she found out that shirley runs this  out of the way bed and breakfast in this  small town in texas  so she is able to sort of like call  around and find out where shirley is  like where the inn is that she runs  and when she talks to shirley on the  phone she finds out that shirley is  actually seems like a lovely person and  is more than welcoming yes please come  out here  so kenzie also hopes that not only will  she be reconnecting with family and have  a place to stay  but because it's sort of out in the  middle of nowhere and she doesn't think  that her boyfriend um knows where it is  uh she's like okay well we're just gonna  escape and he's not gonna know where  we're going and he won't be able to find  us out there so it's win-win so kenzie  and the kids uh get to the sunrise bed  and breakfast  and at first everything just seems  idyllic at first  as usual in these kind of stories  shirley i mean is exactly the kind of  grandmother you could ever hope for that  anyone could ever hope for  uh and she basically offers kenzie and  the kids she's like you can stay here as  long as you need to  and she even agrees like she puts kenzie  to work in the inn you know so she  doesn't feel like she's getting charity  or whatever and she's like look it's  only just me working here so i need help  anyway so you'd be doing me a favor you  know shirley says we don't really have  that many visitors anymore we're kind of  out in the middle of nowhere but we do  have people wandering in from time to  time 